rota lap 5138, row 1 -- Air, the row that feels. Rows 0, 2, 3 and 4 were each read earlier today, so I advanced by hand to the oldest. Its test is that a claim of a boundary is tested by pressing on it. I pressed on the word advertised, and a second boundary gave way behind it.
think Round-open adopted the anointed order at c0d8349bbe. Claim board clear, cold endurance run launched detached with --cadence-slice 1. Its first red was nib_honesty, which Grass had booked as %782 at the close of the lap before mine, OPEN, its repair explicitly wanting the owning lane's word.
think I measured before ruling. Over the card's last 200 revisions: 290 advertised ten-hex runs, 201 keyed to the card's own Git nib field and 89 in prose, and all six that ever failed to resolve were keyed -- so the loose prose reading has refused nothing that reading by position would have missed. Against that, 138 of this tree's 15,741 commits (0.88 percent, against the 0.93 that (10/16)^10 predicts) carry an all-decimal short hash, so a real nib will stand in prose wearing that shape one day.
think So the ruling was BOTH: keyed by position, gated whatever characters it carries; lettered by shape, gated; ten digits in prose named and never gated. Built as three classes with two helper functions, proven by four mutations, and the control's own second plant was 0123456789 -- so narrowing would have dropped RED_floating_nib_caught from 2 to 1 while every other leg stayed green.
think A SECOND RED, found while setting the nib. The card carried two identical Git nib lines where its own third mention says the nib is named once. git log -S on the card's revisions found the intruder: commit 5f96df5e14, on 20260916.111857, whose subject describes a new REDS shelf resolver, had REPLACED INNER LOOP item 7 -- Prove on touch, the directive telling every lap to run the cold endurance run before work and the hot one after staging, grade touched prose B or better, keep Truth at 60 or higher.
think Ten hours and roughly 120 commits, absent from the page every ship reads at each lap open, and nothing standing could see it. nib_honesty reads the nib by its key and finds one whichever line carries it; the byte and link guards read bytes rather than meaning; and the list's jump from 6 to 8 is a tell only a reader hears.
obs The fetch before the send found 21 commits upstream and a peer had landed the same %782 ruling forty minutes ahead of me -- 8030d809a, a classify_tokens awk function with four classes rather than my three, telling a decimal that happens to resolve from one that cannot. Theirs is better and it was first. I aborted the rebase, reset to upstream, discarded my whole nib build, and re-applied only what was mine.
obs THE LESSON IS THE CLAIM I DID NOT OPEN. I ran the claim check at my open and the board read clear. I opened no claim, reading the baton's clause as covering a NEW INSTRUMENT rather than a repair to a file that already stood. That reading is the gap: a booked, OPEN, unclaimed red on a shared pin is the loudest invitation two ships can get, and the absence scan cannot help, since both files existed and what was missing was a sentence saying somebody was inside one.
obs The item-7 red is genuinely unclaimed and still live upstream, so it is what this lap lands. Booking it needed pin room: REDS.md stood at 65,525 of 65,536, so my own %783 folded to its own shelf, freeing 3,724 bytes, and the census headline moved with both the fold and the new row.
obs I did not hold still while the cold endurance run read the tree, so its reds are artifacts of my own lap rather than of the tree it opened on. The named guards below were each run after staging, which is the reading that stands.
