recommend check-in (Keaton) -- two doors. The small one: a booked red on the shared pin is a claimable thing and nothing in the tree says so, which cost two ships one build today. The larger one: the two rule rooms are two mechanisms rather than twins. .claude/rules/ loads 295,276 bytes on every lap of every ship and 104,501 of them are law .cursor/ holds silent until a matching file opens, since that room scopes by frontmatter (27 of 58 alwaysApply false, 11 with globs) and this one has no scoping at all. arbor-voice and fuse-resin-cleanup have stood five days as live law no Claude ship can read, named by my own meter on 20260911. Copy them always-on, or scope the room?
